Problem statement
Sam is curious about Alpha-Hills, so he decided to create Alpha-Hills of different sizes.
An Alpha-hill is represented by a triangle, where alphabets are filled in palindromic order.

For every value of ‘N’, help sam to return the corresponding Alpha-Hill.
Example:

Input: ‘N’ = 3

Output: 
    A
  A B A
A B C B A






public class Solution {
    public static void alphaHill(int n) {
        
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {

            // 1. Fixed spaces: Multiplied by 2 for correct alignment
            for (int s = 1; s <= 2 * (n - i); s++) {
                System.out.print(" ");
            }

            // 2. Fixed character tracking: Declare it OUTSIDE the inner loop
            char c = 'A';
            
            for (int j = 1; j <= 2 * i - 1; j++) {
                System.out.print(c + " ");
                
                // 3. Palindromic logic: Increase until the middle column, then decrease
                if (j < i) {
                    c++; // Going up: A -> B -> C
                } else {
                    c--; // Going down: C -> B -> A
                }
            }

            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}
